{"lessonId":26,"version":"d7184b0c1345","questions":[{"kind":"word-form-choice","sourceId":"v1:part5:26:10","wordId":"collaboration-26","prompt":"The data entry clerk is so accustomed to working by herself that I really doubt if she is capable of ________ on this project.","answer":"collaborating","options":["collaborated","collaborating","collaborator","collaborates"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"word-form-choice","sourceId":"v1:part5:26:11","wordId":"concentrate-26","prompt":"Sue always ________ so hard on her work that she forgets where she is.","answer":"concentrates","options":["concentrated","concentrates","concentration","concentrating"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"word-form-choice","sourceId":"v1:part5:26:12","wordId":"disruption-26","prompt":"The constant flow of traffic by the researcher's desk proved to be very ________","answer":"disruptive","options":["disruptive","disrupts","disruption","disrupted"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"word-form-choice","sourceId":"v1:part5:26:13","wordId":"inconsiderately-26","prompt":"The employee lounge is for everyone's enjoyment so please don't use it ________","answer":"inconsiderately","options":["inconsiderate","inconsiderateness","inconsiderately","inconsideration"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"word-form-choice","sourceId":"v1:part5:26:14","wordId":"opt-26","prompt":"Some people always ________ for the easy way out.","answer":"opt","options":["opt","option","optional","options"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"word-form-choice","sourceId":"v1:part5:26:15","wordId":"scrutiny-26","prompt":"After close ________ of the options, the managers chose an advertising company to do ail the publicity for the new campaign.","answer":"scrutiny","options":["scrutinize","scrutinizing","scrutiny","scrutable"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:adjacent-26:0","wordId":"adjacent-26","prompt":"My office is ________ to the receptionist area on the third floor.","answer":"adjacent","options":["adjacent","lengthy","conducive","apprehensive"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:collaboration-26:1","wordId":"collaboration-26","prompt":"We believe that it was our ________ that enabled us to achieve such favorable results.","answer":"collaboration","options":["collaboration","garment","disruption","goal"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:concentrate-26:0","wordId":"concentrate-26","prompt":"In his quiet, corner office, the manager could finally ________ and finish his work.","answer":"concentrate","options":["concentrate","enhance","conclude","bring up"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:conducive-26:0","wordId":"conducive-26","prompt":"The new office arrangement is much more ________ to work than the dark, depressing space the company had before.","answer":"conducive","options":["conducive","subject to","apprehensive","open to"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:disruption-26:1","wordId":"disruption-26","prompt":"The strike caused a ________ in production at the factory.","answer":"disruption","options":["disruption","defect","brand","research"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:inconsiderately-26:0","wordId":"inconsiderately-26","prompt":"The manager ________ scheduled the meeting for late Friday afternoon.","answer":"inconsiderately","options":["inconsiderately","periodically","systematically","uniformly"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:lobby-26:0","wordId":"lobby-26","prompt":"The salesperson waited in the busy ________ for the buyer to see him.","answer":"lobby","options":["lobby","progress","decade","collaboration"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:move-up-26:1","wordId":"move-up-26","prompt":"In order to ________ in the company, employees had to demonstrate their loyalty.","answer":"move up","options":["move up","lock into","conform","enhance"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:open-to-26:0","wordId":"open-to-26","prompt":"What I valued most in my previous supervisor was that she was always ________ ideas and suggestions.","answer":"open to","options":["open to","anxious","apprehensive","logical"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"},{"kind":"cloze-choice","sourceId":"catalog:example:scrutiny-26:0","wordId":"scrutiny-26","prompt":"After a great deal of ________, the manager decided that the employee's work had improved considerably.","answer":"scrutiny","options":["scrutiny","wrinkle","lobby","agenda"],"sourceVersion":"d7184b0c1345"}]}
